[00:01.06] (Rex Griffin)
[00:11.62] Why do you treat me as if I was only a friend
[00:20.20] What have I done that has made you so different and cold
[00:32.70] Sometimes I wonder if you'll be contented again
[00:43.28] Will you be happy when you are withered and old.
[00:56.22] --- Instrumental ---
[00:56.22] I cannot offer you diamonds or mansions so fine
[01:05.04] I cannot buy you the clothes that your young body crave
[01:16.90] But if you'll say that you long to forever be mine
[01:28.42] Think of the heartaches the sorrow the teardrops you'll save.
[01:47.14] --- Instrumental ---
[01:51.34] When you grow weary and tired of another's caress
[02:00.54] When you are lonely remember this letter my own
[02:11.96] But don't try to answer for there's one thing I'll have to confess
[02:23.32] If you don't love me, I wish you would leave me alone...
